WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:07.675
When a problem has more than one operation, we follow a set order so everyone gets the same answer.

00:08.125 --> 00:16.119
The order is: brackets first. Then multiply and divide, from left to right. Then add and subtract,

00:16.119 --> 00:17.668
from left to right.

00:18.118 --> 00:24.629
In three plus four times two, multiply first. Four times two is eight. Then add:

00:24.629 --> 00:26.826
three plus eight is eleven.

00:27.276 --> 00:34.341
Brackets change the order. In bracket three plus four bracket, times two, do the brackets first.

00:34.341 --> 00:36.401
Seven times two is fourteen.

00:36.851 --> 00:43.190
Same numbers, different order, different answer. That is why the order matters.
